<title>UK: Ex-dividend takes 0.693 points off UK's FTSE index.</title>
<headline>Ex-dividend takes 0.693 points off UK's FTSE index.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>FTSE International said the following FTSE 100 stock went ex-dividend on Monday and the effect was to take 0.693 points off the index in early trading.</p>
<p>						 DIVIDEND   INDEX</p>
<p>						 (PENCE)    EFFECT</p>
<p>		COMPANY			  Net	 Net</p>
<p>* SmithKline Beecham	     4.41	0.693</p>
<p>The net dividend amount includes a Foreign Income Dividend (FID) payment of 2.45p.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
